 ## Overview
-This method reconstructs a triangle mesh from a Signed Distance Function (SDF) by evaluating the field on a grid of cubes, filtering out cubes that are too far from the surface (narrow-band filtering), and applying the standard Marching Cubes algorithm to the remaining cubes [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from naive Marching Cubes implementations by skipping the vast majority of voxels that do not intersect the isosurface, significantly reducing computational cost for sparse or bounded domains [S1, unofficial].
+This method reconstructs a triangle mesh from a Signed Distance Function (SDF) by evaluating the SDF on a regular grid of cubes, filtering out cubes that are too far from the surface (narrow-band filtering), and applying the standard Marching Cubes algorithm only to the intersected cubes [S1, unofficial]. It differs from standard Marching Cubes by skipping the vast majority of the domain volume, significantly reducing computation time for sparse or bounded surfaces [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
-**Inputs and Outputs:**
-*   **Input:** A domain bounding box (`Rect3`), a scalar field function `sdf(Vec3) -> double` (typically an SDF), an `isoLevel` (default 0.0), and optional gradient function `sdfGrad(Vec3) -> Vec3`.
-*   **Output:** A triangle mesh (list of vertices and indices).
+**Inputs:**
+- `domain`: A bounding box defined by `min` (Vec3) and `size` (Vec3).
+- `sdf`: A function `Fun3s` returning a scalar distance for any 3D position.
+- `cubeSize`: The dimensions of each grid cell (Vec3). If not provided, defaults to `domain.size / 50` [S1, unofficial].
+- `isoLevel`: The isovalue for surface extraction, defaulting to 0 [S1, unofficial].
+- `sdfGrad`: An optional gradient function for vertex normals. If `nullptr`, numerical approximation is used [G].
+
+**Outputs:**
+- `mesh`: A triangle mesh containing vertices and indices.
 
 **Data Structures:**
-*   **Cube:** Represents a single voxel in the grid.
-    *   `pos[8]`: Array of 8 vertex coordinates (`Vec3`).
-    *   `sdf[8]`: Array of 8 scalar field values at the vertices (`double`).
-    *   `intersect`: Bitmask or list of intersected edges (derived from `edgeTable`).
-*   **Edge Table:** Standard 256-entry lookup table mapping case indices to 12-bit edge intersection masks [S1, S4, S12, unofficial].
-*   **Triangle Table:** Standard 256x16 lookup table mapping case indices to triangle vertex edge indices [S1, S8, S12, unofficial].
+- `Cube`: Represents a single grid cell.
+  - `pos[8]`: Array of 8 vertex positions (Vec3).
+  - `sdf[8]`: Array of 8 SDF values (double) at the vertices.
+- `signConfigToIntersectedEdges`: A lookup table of 256 integers (12-bit bitmasks). Index is the configuration of signs (positive/negative) at the 8 vertices. Value indicates which of the 12 edges are intersected [S1, unofficial].
+- `edges`: An array of 12 `Edge` structs.
+  - `edgeFlag`: 12-bit integer ($2^i$ for edge $i$).
+  - `vert0`, `vert1`: Indices of the two vertices defining the edge (0-7).
 
-**Parameters:**
-*   `NumCubes`: Integer constant, default 50. Used to determine grid resolution.
-*   `cubeSize`: Derived from `domain.size / NumCubes`.
-*   `isoLevel`: The isovalue for extraction. Default 0.0.
-*   `sdfGrad`: Optional gradient function. If `nullptr`, numerical approximation is used for normals [S1, unofficial].
